findings.description:
"Status is honest" (236-237) cannot be met from the initiative plan alone. In the tested-path input, `001-initiative-plan.squadron.md`:
- line 21 is `[x]` with `Status: in_progress`;
- line 35 is `[x]` with `Status: not_started`;
- line 31 has no status at all;
- line 57 defines the checkbox as "architecture and slice plans complete", not delivered.

"Initiative plan notes" (lines 54-61 of that file) are index bookkeeping, not risks. Either widen the inputs to the `nnn-slices.*.md` checklists and architecture frontmatter, or define a rule for conflicting signals that reports the conflict instead of picking one.

The staleness warning "must appear in the generated document's provenance" (133-135, 334-335). Structural and intent claims must be attributed (143-144). Every overview claim must "trace to an input artifact" (234). None of these has a defined shape:
- frontmatter keys versus a body section, and whether extra keys pass `cf validate frontmatter`;
- which documents carry it, and which fields (graph commit, `lastAnalyzedAt`, `HEAD`, plugin version);
- how an overview with all indices stripped carries a trace at all.

The open question at 341-342 covers only `[INFERRED]` reuse.
